{% doc %}
  Renders a product card (Figma collection grid): a rounded tile with the product image on top, badges
  on the image, then the full title, an optional subtitle and the price.

  Badges (top-left of the image):
  - "Sold out" when no variant can be bought, otherwise "Sale" when the compare-at price is higher.
  - Merchant badges from the product metafield custom.badges ("Badges"): a list of references to
    "Badge" metaobject entries (Content > Metaobjects > Badges). Each entry has a Label and its own
    Background colour and Text colour, so "New" can be cream and "Bestseller" red. One field, so the
    merchant always sets badges the same way, and it can become a clean "Badges" filter (M5).
  Badge colours: an entry's own colours; without them, the default badge colour scheme. Sale and
  Sold out use their own colour schemes (Theme settings > Product cards).
  Subtitle: the product metafield custom.subtitle ("Subtitle", single line text), shown only when
  filled, e.g. "Eau de Parfum · 50ml".
  Both fields are defined once in the admin (Settings > Custom data > Products); see the M3.7 notes.

  The whole card is one link (the title's link stretches over the card), so keyboard users meet one
  stop per product and screen readers hear the product name once.

  Without a product (e.g. a section in the theme editor with no collection chosen yet) it renders a
  placeholder card, so the layout still looks right.

  Tile style (style: 'tile', Figma collection page, M5.2): the photo fills the whole card and the info
  sits on a white strip over its bottom edge. The tile takes the size its parent gives it (a bento grid
  area, or an aspect ratio set by the parent), so it has no image ratio of its own. With show_details,
  hovering the tile (or tabbing into it) slides the strip up to show more:
  - the rating, from Shopify's standard review fields reviews.rating / reviews.rating_count. Review apps
    (Judge.me, Okendo...) fill these; Shopify has no ratings of its own. Hidden when empty.
  - the first words of the product description
  - the quick add button (snippets/quick-add.liquid) and a "View details" label
  Phones and tablets (no hover) keep the short strip: a tap opens the product.

  Full style (style: 'full', the phone design of the collection page, design/collection): the photo on
  top and everything under it, always visible: category line (the product type) and rating, the
  title, the price with a "Save 24%" pill, the first option's values (size pills or colour dots, at most
  6), then the cart button (quick-add) and BUY. BUY is a link to Shopify's cart permalink
  (/cart/<variant id>:1), which opens the checkout with that one product: no second form per card.
  Sold out: "Notify me", a link to the product page (back-in-stock is an app, decision 6).
  The option values are real choices (radios) only when the product has ONE option: choosing one swaps
  the price (a <template> rendered by snippets/price.liquid, so labels and the unit price stay right),
  the cart button's variant and the BUY link, or shows Notify me for a sold-out value. With several
  options they only show which values exist.

  @param {product} [product] - The product. Leave empty for a placeholder card
  @param {string} [style] - 'card' (default: image on top, info below), 'tile' or 'full' (see above)
  @param {string} [image_ratio] - Card style: 'portrait' (4:5, default), 'square', 'landscape' (4:3) or 'original'
  @param {string} [sizes] - The image's sizes attribute. Default: 4 per row on desktop, 2 on phones
  @param {string} [loading] - 'eager' or 'lazy' to override the image snippet's automatic choice
  @param {boolean} [priority] - true for the page's largest image (LCP): eager + fetchpriority high
  @param {boolean} [show_secondary_image] - Show the second product image on hover (default false)
  @param {string} [heading_tag] - Tag for the title, default 'h3'
  @param {boolean} [show_details] - Tile style: reveal the details panel on hover / keyboard focus
  @param {boolean} [show_rating] - Details panel: show the review rating when an app provides one
  @param {boolean} [show_description] - Details panel: show the start of the description
  @param {string} [cart_options] - Details panel quick add, products with several variants: 'add_first' or 'link'
  @param {string} [id_suffix] - Added to the quick add form id (with the card style), so the same product
    two times in one section gives two different ids (e.g. 'picks' for a second list of products)

  Buttons (Theme settings > Product cards > Buttons, for the Full card and the Tile panel): the BUY
  text and icon, and the cart button: round with an icon (default) or a pill with text, with the
  default cart icon, a custom image or (pill only) no icon.

  @example
  {% render 'product-card', product: product %}
  {% render 'product-card', product: product, image_ratio: 'square', show_secondary_image: true %}
  {% render 'product-card', product: product, style: 'tile', show_details: true, show_rating: true, show_description: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign card_style = style | default: 'card'
  assign ratio = image_ratio | default: 'portrait'
  assign image_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 990px) 25vw, 50vw'
  assign title_tag = heading_tag | default: 'h3'

  # Buttons (Theme settings > Product cards > Buttons). Empty texts = the default texts (locales)
  assign buy_label = 'products.card.buy' | t
  if settings.card_buy_label != blank
    assign buy_label = settings.card_buy_label
  endif
  assign cart_text = false
  if settings.card_cart_style == 'text'
    assign cart_text = true
  endif
  assign cart_label = settings.card_cart_label
  assign cart_icon_image = nil
  if settings.card_cart_icon == 'custom' and settings.card_cart_icon_image != blank
    assign cart_icon_image = settings.card_cart_icon_image
  endif
  # "No icon" only for the pill: the round button keeps the default icon
  assign cart_show_icon = true
  if cart_text and settings.card_cart_icon == 'none'
    assign cart_show_icon = false
  endif

  # Quick add form id: the card style (so two card styles of one product in one section never share an
  # id) and the caller's suffix
  assign quick_add_suffix = card_style
  if id_suffix != blank
    assign quick_add_suffix = quick_add_suffix | append: '-' | append: id_suffix
  endif

  assign image_class = ''
  if ratio != 'original'
    assign image_class = 'image--cover'
  endif

  # A tile always fills its box: the photo is cropped to the tile's shape
  assign media_class = 'product-card__media--' | append: ratio
  if card_style == 'tile'
    assign image_class = 'image--cover'
    assign media_class = 'product-card__media--fill'
  endif
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    # Second image for the hover swap: only when asked for and the product has one
    assign secondary_image = nil
    if show_secondary_image and product.media.size > 1
      assign secondary_image = product.media[1].preview_image
    endif

    assign on_sale = false
    if product.compare_at_price > product.price
      assign on_sale = true
    endif

    # Rating (tile details and the full card): Shopify's standard review fields, filled by a review app.
    # .value of a rating field is a rating object: .rating (e.g. 4.9) and .scale_max (e.g. 5).
    assign rating = nil
    if show_rating
      assign rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
      assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | default: 0
      # scale_max is stored as "5.0": round it so screen readers hear "out of 5"
      assign rating_max = rating.scale_max | round
    endif
  -%}
  {%- capture rating_markup -%}
    {%- if rating != blank -%}
      <p class="product-card__rating">
        <span class="product-card__stars" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- rating.rating | round: 1 }} <span class="product-card__star">★</span>
        </span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">
          {{- 'products.card.rating' | t: rating: rating.rating, max: rating_max -}}
        </span>
        {%- if rating_count > 0 -%}
          <span class="product-card__reviews">{{ 'products.card.reviews_count' | t: count: rating_count }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if card_style == 'full' -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
        # The option the card shows: the FIRST option (user, 2026-11-25: preferring the color option made
        # every test product show "red / blue" and hid sizes). Its values are choices on every product
        # with options: a value = the first in-stock variant with that value (else the first one with
        # it); the other options are chosen on the product page
        assign card_option = product.options_with_values.first
        assign option_key = 'option' | append: card_option.position
        assign options_interactive = false
        unless product.has_only_default_variant
          assign options_interactive = true
        endunless

        # Only 6 values show: the card's variant must be one of them (the first in stock, else the
        # first), so the price and BUY never belong to a value the shopper can't see
        if options_interactive
          assign value_variants = product.variants | where: option_key, card_option.values.first.name
          assign variant = value_variants.first
          for value in card_option.values limit: 6
            assign value_variants = product.variants | where: option_key, value.name
            assign in_stock = value_variants | where: 'available' | first
            if in_stock
              assign variant = in_stock
              break
            endif
          endfor
        endif

        # #9: a price <template> per value only when the values cost different amounts
        assign price_templates = false
        if product.price_varies or product.compare_at_price_varies
          assign price_templates = true
        endif

        # "Save 24%": the first variant's saving (the script updates it with the chosen value)
        assign save_percent = 0
        if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
          assign save_percent = variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: variant.compare_at_price | round
        endif

        assign buy_url = routes.cart_url | append: '/' | append: variant.id | append: ':1'
        assign card_id = 'Card-' | append: product.id | append: '-' | append: section.id
    -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- liquid
    # Full card with 2+ media: the photo slider (swipe, dots, arrows on hover; at most 5 images). The
    # second-image hover swap is off then. Every slide uses the media's preview image, so a video or a
    # 3D model shows its poster (Theme Store: rich media must not break the card)
    assign has_slider = false
    if card_style == 'full' and product.media.size > 1
      assign has_slider = true
      assign secondary_image = nil
      assign slide_count = product.media.size | at_most: 5
    endif

    # The photo box's height as a share of the card width: the "Add to cart" pill sits on its bottom
    # edge (desktop hover layout). 'original' = the first image's own shape
    assign card_style_attr = ''
    if card_style == 'full'
      case ratio
        when 'square'
          assign media_h = 1
        when 'landscape'
          assign media_h = 0.75
        when 'original'
          # No image (aspect_ratio empty): the portrait shape, never a division by nothing
          assign media_h = 1.25
          assign first_ratio = product.featured_media.preview_image.aspect_ratio | default: 0
          if first_ratio > 0
            assign media_h = 1.0 | divided_by: first_ratio
          endif
        else
          assign media_h = 1.25
      endcase
      assign card_style_attr = '--card-media-h: ' | append: media_h | append: ';'
      # A slider needs one shape for every slide: 'original' = the first image's shape, cropped
      if has_slider and ratio == 'original'
        assign media_aspect = product.featured_media.preview_image.aspect_ratio | default: 0.8
        assign card_style_attr = card_style_attr | append: ' --card-media-ratio: ' | append: media_aspect | append: ';'
        assign image_class = 'image--cover'
      endif
    endif
  -%}

  <div
    class="product-card product-card--{{ card_style }}{% if secondary_image %} product-card--has-secondary{% endif %}{% unless product.available %} product-card--sold-out{% endunless %}"
    {% if card_style_attr != blank %}
      style="{{ card_style_attr }}"
    {% endif %}
  >
    <div class="product-card__media {{ media_class }}{% if has_slider %} product-card__media--slider{% endif %}">
      {%- if has_slider -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Each slide is a link to the product (tabindex -1, hidden from screen readers: the title link
          names the product once). The track sits above the title link's stretched box, so a swipe moves
          the photos. Arrows and dots are mouse / touch helpers (no tab stops: 24 cards would add 48)
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <card-gallery class="product-card__gallery">
          <div class="product-card__slides" data-card-slides>
            {%- for media in product.media limit: 5 -%}
              <a class="product-card__slide" href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-media-id="{{ media.id }}">
                {%- if forloop.first -%}
                  {% render 'image', image: media.preview_image, class: image_class, sizes: image_sizes, alt: '', loading: loading, priority: priority %}
                {%- else -%}
                  {% render 'image', image: media.preview_image, class: image_class, sizes: image_sizes, alt: '', loading: 'lazy' %}
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
          <span class="product-card__arrow product-card__arrow--prev" data-card-prev aria-hidden="true">
            {{- 'icon-chevron.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
          </span>
          <span class="product-card__arrow product-card__arrow--next" data-card-next aria-hidden="true">
            {{- 'icon-chevron.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
          </span>
          <span class="product-card__dots" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for i in (1..slide_count) -%}
              <span class="product-card__dot{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}" data-card-dot="{{ forloop.index0 }}"></span>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </span>
        </card-gallery>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- liquid
          # The image is decorative here (alt=""): the title link right below names the product, so a
          # screen reader would otherwise hear the name twice.
          render 'image', image: product.featured_media.preview_image, class: image_class, sizes: image_sizes, alt: '', loading: loading, priority: priority
          if secondary_image
            render 'image', image: secondary_image, class: 'image--cover product-card__secondary', sizes: image_sizes, alt: '', loading: 'lazy'
          endif
        -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="product-card__badges">
        {%- if card_style == 'full' -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Full card (design): the product's own badges first (Trending, New), then the discount ("-30%",
            the same number as the "Save" pill; the script follows the chosen value). Sold out: its badge
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% render 'product-badges', field: product.metafields.custom.badges %}
          {%- if product.available == false -%}
            <span class="product-card__badge color-{{ settings.sold_out_badge_color_scheme.id }}">{{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span
            class="product-card__badge product-card__badge--discount color-{{ settings.sale_badge_color_scheme.id }}"
            data-card-discount
            data-template="{{ 'products.card.discount' | t: percent: '[percent]' | escape }}"
            {% if save_percent == 0 %}
              hidden
            {% endif %}
          >
            {{- 'products.card.discount' | t: percent: save_percent -}}
          </span>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if product.available == false -%}
            <span class="product-card__badge color-{{ settings.sold_out_badge_color_scheme.id }}">{{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}</span>
          {%- elsif on_sale -%}
            <span class="product-card__badge color-{{ settings.sale_badge_color_scheme.id }}">{{ 'products.badge.sale' | t }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The product's "Badges" field (custom.badges): snippets/product-badges reads it (list or single
            value) and draws each badge (own colours for a Badge metaobject entry, else the default badge
            colour scheme).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% render 'product-badges', field: product.metafields.custom.badges %}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if card_style == 'full' -%}
      <card-options class="product-card__body" data-cart-url="{{ routes.cart_url }}">
        <div class="product-card__meta">
          {%- comment -%} The product type only (the design's short "SKINCARE" line); the subtitle can be a whole sentence {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if product.type != blank -%}
            <p class="product-card__category">{{ product.type | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if rating != blank -%}
            {%- liquid
              # Design: "★ 4.9 (1.2k)": the count short from 1000 (1234 -> 1.2k)
              assign count_short = rating_count
              if rating_count >= 1000
                assign count_whole = rating_count | divided_by: 1000
                assign count_tenth = rating_count | divided_by: 100 | modulo: 10
                assign count_short = count_whole | append: 'k'
                if count_tenth > 0
                  assign count_short = count_whole | append: '.' | append: count_tenth | append: 'k'
                endif
              endif
            -%}
            <p class="product-card__score">
              <span aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="product-card__star">★</span> {{ rating.rating | round: 1 -}}
                {%- if rating_count > 0 %} ({{ count_short }}){% endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="visually-hidden">
                {{- 'products.card.rating' | t: rating: rating.rating, max: rating_max -}}
                {%- if rating_count > 0 %}, {{ 'products.card.reviews_count' | t: count: rating_count }}{% endif -%}
              </span>
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <{{ title_tag }} class="product-card__title">
          <a class="product-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
        </{{ title_tag }}>

        <div class="product-card__pricing">
          <div data-card-price>{% render 'price', product: product, variant: variant %}</div>
          <span
            class="product-card__save"
            data-card-save
            data-template="{{ 'products.card.save' | t: percent: '[percent]' | escape }}"
            {% if save_percent == 0 %}
              hidden
            {% endif %}
          >
            {{- 'products.card.save' | t: percent: save_percent -}}
          </span>
        </div>

        {%- if options_interactive -%}
          <fieldset class="product-card__options">
            <legend class="visually-hidden">{{ card_option.name | escape }}</legend>
            {%- for value in card_option.values limit: 6 -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign value_variants = product.variants | where: option_key, value.name
                assign value_variant = value_variants | where: 'available' | first
                unless value_variant
                  assign value_variant = value_variants.first
                endunless
                assign input_id = card_id | append: '-' | append: forloop.index
                assign value_save = 0
                if value_variant.compare_at_price > value_variant.price
                  assign value_save = value_variant.compare_at_price | minus: value_variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: value_variant.compare_at_price | round
                endif
                assign value_add_name = product.title | append: ' - ' | append: value_variant.title

                # A text pill; a colour dot only when the value has a Shopify swatch (Products > the
                # product > the option's values: a colour or an image, e.g. lipstick shades)
                assign value_look = 'text'
                if value.swatch.color or value.swatch.image
                  assign value_look = 'swatch'
                endif

                # The photo to show: its slide (first 5 media), else a <template> the script swaps in
                assign value_media = value_variant.featured_media
                assign value_media_template = false
                if value_media
                  if has_slider == false
                    assign value_media_template = true
                  elsif value_media.position > 5
                    assign value_media_template = true
                  endif
                endif
              -%}
              <input
                class="visually-hidden"
                type="radio"
                id="{{ input_id }}"
                name="{{ card_id }}"
                value="{{ value_variant.id }}"
                data-available="{{ value_variant.available }}"
                data-save="{{ value_save }}"
                data-add-name="{{ value_add_name | escape }}"
                data-add-label="{{ 'products.quick_add.add' | t: title: value_add_name | escape }}"
                data-added-label="{{ 'products.quick_add.added' | t: title: value_add_name | escape }}"
                {% if value_media %}
                  data-media-id="{{ value_media.id }}"
                {% endif %}
                {% if value_variant.id == variant.id %}
                  checked
                {% endif %}
              >
              <label
                class="product-card__option product-card__option--{{ value_look }}{% unless value_variant.available %} product-card__option--sold-out{% endunless %}"
                for="{{ input_id }}"
                {% if value_look != 'text' %}
                  title="{{ value.name | escape }}"
                {% endif %}
                {% if value_look == 'swatch' and value.swatch.color %}
                  style="--swatch-color: {{ value.swatch.color }};"
                {% endif %}
              >
                {%- case value_look -%}
                  {%- when 'swatch' -%}
                    {%- if value.swatch.image -%}
                      {{ value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 48 | image_tag: alt: '', loading: 'lazy' }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    <span class="visually-hidden">{{ value.name | escape }}</span>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{- value.name | escape -}}
                {%- endcase -%}
              </label>
              {%- if price_templates -%}
                <template data-price-for="{{ value_variant.id }}">{% render 'price', product: product, variant: value_variant %}</template>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if value_media_template -%}
                <template data-media-for="{{ value_media.id }}">
                  {%- render 'image', image: value_media.preview_image, class: image_class, sizes: image_sizes, alt: '', loading: 'lazy' -%}
                </template>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </fieldset>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="product-card__buy">
          {%- if product.available -%}
            <div class="product-card__buy-now{% if cart_text %} product-card__buy-now--text{% endif %}" data-card-buy>
              {%- comment -%}
                One cart button, always the text pill ("Add to cart" + the product name for screen readers).
                Cart button style "round" (default): on phones / tablets the CSS shows it as a round icon
                (the text visually hidden), on a desktop card with a mouse it is the "ADD TO CART" pill that
                appears over the photo on hover (design). "With text": the text pill everywhere.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign quick_add_class = 'product-card__quick-add'
                if cart_text
                  assign quick_add_class = quick_add_class | append: ' product-card__cart-text'
                else
                  assign quick_add_class = quick_add_class | append: ' product-card__quick-add--icon'
                endif
              -%}
              {% render 'quick-add',
                product: product,
                style: 'pill',
                size: 44,
                label: cart_label,
                icon_image: cart_icon_image,
                show_icon: cart_show_icon,
                options: 'add_first',
                class: quick_add_class,
                id_suffix: quick_add_suffix
              %}
              <a class="button product-card__buy-link" href="{{ buy_url }}" data-card-buy-link>
                {%- case settings.card_buy_icon -%}
                  {%- when 'none' -%}
                  {%- when 'custom' -%}
                    {%- if settings.card_buy_icon_image != blank -%}
                      {{- settings.card_buy_icon_image | image_url: width: 48 | image_tag: alt: '', loading: 'lazy' -}}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{- 'icon-buy-now.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{- 'icon-buy-now.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                {%- endcase -%}
                <span class="product-card__buy-label">{{ buy_label | escape }}</span>
                {%- comment -%} One line: no space before the colon in the name ("Buy: Serum") {%- endcomment -%}
                <span class="visually-hidden">: {{ product.title | escape }}</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          <a
            class="button button--secondary product-card__notify"
            href="{{ product.url }}"
            data-card-notify
            {% if product.available %}
              hidden
            {% endif %}
          >
            {{- 'icon-bell.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            {{- 'products.card.notify' | t -}}
            <span class="visually-hidden">: {{ product.title | escape }}</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </card-options>
    {%- else -%}
    <div class="product-card__panel">
      <div class="product-card__info">
        <div class="product-card__text">
          <{{ title_tag }} class="product-card__title">
            <a class="product-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
          </{{ title_tag }}>
          {%- assign subtitle = product.metafields.custom.subtitle.value -%}
          {%- if subtitle != blank -%}
            <p class="product-card__subtitle">{{ subtitle | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {% render 'price', product: product %}
      </div>

      {%- if card_style == 'tile' and show_details -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign description = ''
          if show_description
            assign description = product.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncatewords: 16
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="product-card__details">
          <div class="product-card__details-inner">
            {{- rating_markup -}}

            {%- if description != blank -%}
              <p class="product-card__description">{{ description }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Above the stretched link (z-index), so the cart button gets the click. "View details" is a
              label only: the whole tile is already the link to the product.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- liquid
              # With text: a product with several variants and cart_options 'link' can't be added from
              # the card, so the pill would only be a second "View details" link (quick-add's fallback).
              # No pill then: the "View details" label stays and the whole tile is the link.
              assign pill_links_only = false
              if cart_text and product.available and product.variants.size > 1 and cart_options == 'link'
                assign pill_links_only = true
              endif
            -%}
            <div class="product-card__actions">
              {%- if pill_links_only -%}
              {%- elsif cart_text -%}
                {% render 'quick-add',
                  product: product,
                  style: 'pill',
                  size: 44,
                  label: cart_label,
                  icon_image: cart_icon_image,
                  show_icon: cart_show_icon,
                  options: cart_options,
                  class: 'product-card__cart-text',
                  id_suffix: quick_add_suffix
                %}
              {%- else -%}
                {% render 'quick-add', product: product, size: 44, icon_color: '#7d0000', icon_image: cart_icon_image, options: cart_options, id_suffix: quick_add_suffix %}
              {%- endif -%}
              <span class="product-card__more" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="product-card__more-label">{{ 'products.card.view_details' | t }}</span>
                {{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%} Placeholder card: same layout, sample content, no link {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="product-card product-card--{{ card_style }} product-card--placeholder">
    <div class="product-card__media {{ media_class }}">
      {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'product-card__placeholder' }}
    </div>
    <div class="product-card__panel">
      <div class="product-card__info">
        <div class="product-card__text">
          <{{ title_tag }} class="product-card__title">{{ 'products.card.placeholder_title' | t }}</{{ title_tag }}>
        </div>
        <div class="price"><span class="price__current">{{ 2100 | money }}</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    Figma card: a white glass tile, small rounded corners (19px), soft shadow; image on top, then the
    title + subtitle on the left and the red price on the right.
  */
  .product-card {
    position: relative; /* the title link's ::after stretches over the whole card */
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--color-glass-strong);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-frost));
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-frost));
  }

  /* Keyboard focus: the ring goes around the whole card, not just the title text */
  .product-card:has(.product-card__link:focus-visible) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .product-card__link:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
  }

  .product-card__media {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .product-card__media--portrait {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
  }

  .product-card__media--square {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
  }

  .product-card__media--landscape {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  }

  .product-card__media .image > img {
    transition:
      transform var(--duration-slow) var(--ease-out),
      opacity var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  /* Hover: a slow, gentle zoom; with a second image, that one fades in on top */
  .product-card:hover .product-card__media .image > img {
    transform: scale(1.04);
  }

  .product-card__secondary {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }

  .product-card__secondary > img {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .product-card--has-secondary:hover .product-card__secondary > img {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .product-card__media .image > img {
      transition: none;
    }

    .product-card:hover .product-card__media .image > img {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .product-card__placeholder {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    background-color: var(--color-tint-subtle);
    fill: var(--color-tint-border);
  }

  /*
    Badges top-left of the image. Figma: a cream rounded rectangle with red text ("New").
    Colours come from the colour scheme chosen in Theme settings > Product cards: the scheme class
    (color-scheme-N) paints the scheme's background; the text uses the scheme's accent.
  */
  .product-card__badges {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: var(--space-sm);
    inset-inline-start: var(--space-sm);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .product-card__badge {
    padding: 0.3em 0.75em;
    border-radius: 0.75em;
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  /*
    Two classes on purpose: the scheme class sets color: var(--color-text) with one class, and which
    stylesheet loads last isn't guaranteed. Two classes always win, so the text is the scheme's accent.
  */
  .product-card .product-card__badge {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* A badge entry with its own colours (Content > Metaobjects > Badges); three classes beat the rule above */
  .product-card .product-card__badge.product-card__badge--own-colors {
    background-color: var(--badge-bg);
    color: var(--badge-fg);
  }

  /* Title + subtitle left, price right; the price drops below on a narrow card */
  .product-card__info {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
  }

  .product-card__text {
    flex: 1 1 10rem;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .product-card__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .product-card__link {
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* The stretched link: an invisible box over the whole card, so a click anywhere opens the product */
  .product-card__link::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .product-card__subtitle {
    margin: var(--space-2xs) 0 0;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 70%, var(--color-background));
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
  }

  .product-card .price {
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm);
  }

  /*
    ---------- Tile style (Figma collection page) ----------
    A white tile with a 4px frame; the photo fills it and the white info strip sits over the photo's
    bottom edge. The tile fills the box its parent gives it (block-size: 100%).
    Layers: isolation makes the tile its own stacking context, so the photo can sit at z-index -1
    (under the strip) while the stretched title link (z-index 1) still covers the whole tile, and the
    cart button (z-index 2) sits above that.
    container-type: size lets short tiles drop the description (container query below).
  */
  .product-card--tile {
    isolation: isolate;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    block-size: 100%;
    padding: 0.25rem;
    border: 0;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 5px 25px 0 #0000000d; /* Figma collection-card shadow */
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
    backdrop-filter: none;
    container-type: size;
  }

  .product-card__media--fill {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0.25rem;
    z-index: -1;
    border-radius: calc(var(--radius-sm) - 0.25rem);
  }

  .product-card__media--fill > .image {
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  /* Badges a little further in, like the Figma ("Trending" sits ~24px from the corner) */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__badges {
    inset-block-start: var(--space-lg);
    inset-inline-start: var(--space-lg);
  }

  /*
    The details strip is glass over the photo (Figma Glass: Light -45deg 80%, Frost 157.25; drop shadow
    0 0 14.77px #000000 5%).
    - Light -45deg = the light comes from the top LEFT: a bright 1px rim on the top and left edges (80%
      white) and a weaker one bottom-right.
    - Frost: the theme maps Frost 100 to a 35px blur, so 157.25 = 35px x 1.5725 = 55px.
    - The fill is the theme's strong glass (50% white), so the text stays readable on any photo.
    Figma's Refraction, Depth, Dispersion and Splay bend light through the glass; CSS has no equivalent,
    so the blur, rim and shadow carry the effect.
  */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__panel {
    border-radius: calc(var(--radius-sm) - 0.25rem);
    background-color: var(--color-glass-strong);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 14.77px 0 #0000000d,
      inset 1px 1px 0 #ffffffcc,
      inset -1px -1px 0 #ffffff80;
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(55px);
    backdrop-filter: blur(55px);
  }

  /* Strip: title + subtitle left, price right and vertically centred (Figma: ~103px tall at 1920px) */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
  }

  /*
    The glass blur (backdrop-filter) makes the strip the box that absolutely positioned children measure
    from, so the title link's click area (::after, inset: 0) would only cover the strip. The tile is a
    size container, so 100cqh = the tile's full height: the click area hangs from the strip's bottom
    edge and reaches the top of the tile again (-0.25rem = the tile's white frame).
  */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__link::after {
    inset: auto -0.25rem -0.25rem;
    block-size: 100cqh;
  }

  .product-card--tile .product-card__title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  /*
    Price on the right edge. The price lines are stacked in a column, right-aligned: as a wrapping row,
    the unit price line (flex-basis 100%) made the box as wide as both lines side by side, so the price
    started mid-card and squeezed the title.
  */
  .product-card--tile .price {
    flex: 0 1 auto;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-end;
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-lg);
    text-align: end;
  }

  .product-card--tile .price__unit {
    flex-basis: auto;
  }

  .product-card--tile .price__current {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /*
    Details panel: folded away (0fr) until the tile is hovered or something inside has keyboard focus,
    then it grows to its natural height (1fr) and the strip slides up over the photo. visibility keeps
    the folded content away from screen readers and the Tab key; tabbing onto the title link opens the
    panel first (focus-within), so the cart button is visible before it gets focus.
  */
  .product-card__details {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    transition: grid-template-rows var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .product-card__details-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    min-block-size: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-inline: var(--space-lg);
    visibility: hidden;
    transition: visibility 0s linear var(--duration-base);
  }

  .product-card--tile:focus-within .product-card__details {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }

  .product-card--tile:focus-within .product-card__details-inner {
    visibility: visible;
    transition-delay: 0s;
  }

  /* Hover only where there is a real pointer: on touch screens a tap goes straight to the product */
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .product-card--tile:hover .product-card__details {
      grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    }

    .product-card--tile:hover .product-card__details-inner {
      visibility: visible;
      transition-delay: 0s;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .product-card__details {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  /* "4.9 ★  213 reviews": number + gold star, then the count in a soft pill */
  .product-card__rating {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  }

  .product-card__star {
    color: #c8a24b;
  }

  .product-card__reviews {
    padding: 0.15em 0.6em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: var(--color-tint-subtle);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .product-card__description {
    display: -webkit-box;
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 70%, var(--color-background));
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    line-clamp: 2;
  }

  .product-card__actions {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2; /* above the stretched title link */
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap; /* a long cart button text puts "View details" on the next line */
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-md);
    pointer-events: none; /* clicks on "View details" and the gaps fall through to the stretched link */
  }

  .product-card__actions .quick-add {
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  /*
    The glass cart button needs something behind it to show; on the white strip it gets a soft tint
    instead (three classes beat quick-add's own two-class rule).
  */
  .product-card__actions .quick-add:where(:not(.quick-add--pill)) .quick-add__button {
    background-color: var(--color-tint);
  }

  /* "View details": a label in the Figma pill style; the whole tile is the link */
  .product-card__more {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    block-size: 2.5rem;
    padding-inline: var(--space-lg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-background);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    pointer-events: none; /* clicks fall through to the stretched link */
  }

  .product-card__more svg {
    display: none;
    inline-size: 1rem;
    block-size: 1rem;
  }

  /* Tiles: the subtitle is always one line ("…"), so the strip keeps the same height */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__subtitle {
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Short tiles (e.g. 1280px screens, the shortest bento tiles): no description, so the panel fits */
  @container (max-height: 24rem) {
    .product-card__description {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /*
    Very short tiles (the bento's 1-column tiles on 1200-1440px screens are ~190-220px tall): a compact
    strip, one line each for title and price, no subtitle, so the photo still shows (~1/3 strip, as in the
    Figma at 1920px).
  */
  @container (max-height: 16rem) {
    .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
      padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__title {
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__subtitle {
      display: none;
    }

    .product-card--tile .price {
      font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    }

    .product-card--tile .price__unit {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /*
    Narrow tiles, measured on the tile itself (a size container), so it works wherever the card sits.
    - Up to 24rem (phones, small bento tiles): "View details" becomes a round arrow button; the label
      wrapped onto two lines here.
    - Up to 20rem (the 1-column bento tiles on small laptops): the price goes under the title instead of
      beside it, so the title gets the full width and words never break letter by letter.
  */
  @container (max-width: 24rem) {
    .product-card__more {
      justify-content: center;
      inline-size: 2.75rem;
      block-size: 2.75rem;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .product-card__more-label {
      display: none;
    }

    .product-card__more svg {
      display: block;
    }
  }

  @container (max-width: 20rem) {
    .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: flex-start;
      row-gap: var(--space-2xs);
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__text {
      flex: 1 1 100%;
    }

    .product-card--tile .price {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-xs);
      margin-inline-start: 0;
      font-size: var(--font-size-body);
      text-align: start;
    }
  }

  /*
    Phones (one tile per row): a slimmer strip, so the photo keeps most of the tile. Title up to 2 lines,
    price at body size; the text column gets the room and never breaks mid-word.
  */
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
      gap: var(--space-sm);
      padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__text {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__title {
      display: -webkit-box;
      overflow: hidden;
      -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
      -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
      line-clamp: 2;
    }

    .product-card--tile .price {
      flex: none;
      font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    }
  }
  /*
    ---------- Full style (phone design of the collection page) ----------
    Photo on top, everything under it. The controls (options, cart, BUY, Notify me) sit above the
    stretched title link (z-index 2), so they get the clicks; the rest of the card opens the product.
  */
  .product-card__body {
    display: flex;
    flex: 1;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
  }

  .product-card__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-xs);
  }

  .product-card__category {
    overflow: hidden;
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-inline-size: 0;
    margin: 0;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .product-card__score {
    flex: none;
    margin: 0;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 75%, var(--color-background));
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .product-card__pricing {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .product-card--full .price {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  }

  .product-card__save {
    padding: 0.2em 0.7em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 10%, var(--color-background));
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
  }

  .product-card__save[hidden],
  .product-card__buy-now[hidden],
  .product-card__notify[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .product-card__options {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* Size pills: the chosen one dark (design), a sold-out one struck through */
  .product-card__option {
    display: inline-block;
    overflow: hidden;
    max-inline-size: 100%;
    padding: 0.3em 0.7em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 30%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  :checked + .product-card__option {
    border-color: var(--color-text);
    background-color: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-background);
  }

  :focus-visible + .product-card__option {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* 65%: grey text needs at least a 62% mix for 4.5:1 (55% gave 3.74:1); the value can still be picked (Notify me) */
  .product-card__option--sold-out {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 65%, transparent);
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }

  /* Colour dots (the option has swatches): a ring shows the chosen one */
  .product-card__option--swatch {
    overflow: hidden;
    inline-size: 1.5rem;
    min-block-size: 0;
    block-size: 1.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-background);
    background-color: var(--swatch-color, var(--color-tint));
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 25%, transparent);
  }

  :checked + .product-card__option--swatch {
    border-color: var(--color-background);
    background-color: var(--swatch-color, var(--color-tint));
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--color-text);
  }

  .product-card__option--swatch img {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  /* A sold-out dot: faded (a line can't cross a dot) */
  .product-card__option--sold-out.product-card__option--swatch {
    opacity: 0.45;
  }

  /*
    ---------- Full card: photo slider (design 2026-11-25) ----------
    The track scrolls sideways with snap points (swipe on touch). It sits above the title link's
    stretched box (z-index 2), so a swipe moves the photos; each slide is itself a link to the product.
    Arrows (hover) and dots are mouse / touch helpers; badges and the cart pill sit above the track.
  */
  /* "Original" shape with a slider: every slide takes the first photo's shape (the others: their ratio class) */
  .product-card__media--original.product-card__media--slider {
    aspect-ratio: var(--card-media-ratio, 0.8);
  }

  .product-card__gallery {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 2;
    display: block;
  }

  .product-card__slides {
    display: flex;
    block-size: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }

  .product-card__slides::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  .product-card__slide {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 100%;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }

  .product-card__slide .image {
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  .product-card--full .product-card__badges {
    z-index: 3;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .product-card__badge[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Dots (design): white, the shown photo a longer pill */
  .product-card__dots {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-end: var(--space-sm);
    inset-inline: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .product-card__dot {
    inline-size: 0.375rem;
    block-size: 0.375rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: #ffffffa6;
    box-shadow: 0 0 2px #00000040;
    cursor: pointer;
    pointer-events: auto;
    transition: inline-size var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .product-card__dot.is-active {
    inline-size: 1.25rem;
    background-color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* Arrows: only with a mouse, shown while the card is hovered */
  .product-card__arrow {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: 50%;
    z-index: 1;
    display: none;
    place-items: center;
    inline-size: 2rem;
    block-size: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-background) 88%, transparent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-button);
    color: var(--color-text);
    cursor: pointer;
    opacity: 0;
    translate: 0 -50%;
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .product-card__arrow svg {
    inline-size: 0.75rem;
    block-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .product-card__arrow--prev {
    inset-inline-start: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .product-card__arrow--next {
    inset-inline-end: var(--space-xs);
  }

  /* The theme's chevron points down: next turns to point to the end side, prev to the start side */
  .product-card__arrow--next svg {
    rotate: -90deg;
  }

  .product-card__arrow--prev svg {
    rotate: 90deg;
  }

  .product-card__arrow--next:dir(rtl) svg {
    rotate: 90deg;
  }

  .product-card__arrow--prev:dir(rtl) svg {
    rotate: -90deg;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .product-card__arrow {
      display: grid;
    }

    .product-card:hover .product-card__arrow {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  .product-card__arrow:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* Sold out (design): the photo fades */
  .product-card--sold-out .product-card__media :is(.image, .product-card__slides) {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /*
    ---------- Full card: buy row ----------
    The card is a size container, so the layout follows the card's own width (any column count):
    - small (under 15rem, 2 per row on phones): price, options, then the cart circle (left) + BUY (right)
    - medium (15rem and wider, touch screens): price, then options (left) + cart circle + BUY (right)
    - large (15rem and wider with a mouse): options, then price + BUY in one row; the cart button is the
      "ADD TO CART" pill that appears over the bottom of the photo on hover (design)
  */
  .product-card--full {
    container: product-card / inline-size;
  }

  .product-card__buy {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    margin-block-start: auto;
    padding-block-start: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .product-card__buy-now {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  /*
    Cart circle and BUY as one pair, both 44px tall. Two classes: the global .button rule loads after
    this file and beat the one-class rule (height, padding)
  */
  .product-card .product-card__buy-link,
  .product-card .product-card__notify {
    gap: 0.4em;
    min-block-size: 2.75rem;
    padding-block: 0;
    padding-inline: 1.1rem;
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
  }

  .product-card__notify {
    inline-size: 100%;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .product-card__buy-link :is(svg, img),
  .product-card__notify svg {
    flex: none;
    inline-size: 1.1em;
    block-size: 1.1em;
  }

  /* The BUY cart icon is drawn small in its box: 1.25rem (20px), the same as the cart circle's icon */
  .product-card .product-card__buy-link svg {
    inline-size: 1.25rem;
    block-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .product-card__buy-link img {
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  /*
    BUY keeps its width (flex: none) and wraps only between words: "anywhere" broke "BUY" into B / U / Y
    (and BU / Y at 390px) when the row was short
  */
  .product-card__buy-link {
    flex: none;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .product-card__buy-label {
    overflow-wrap: normal;
  }

  /* The cart button in its round look ("round" style): the text visually hidden, a 44px circle */
  .product-card .product-card__quick-add--icon .quick-add__button {
    flex: none;
    inline-size: var(--quick-add-size, 2.75rem);
    min-inline-size: 0;
    block-size: var(--quick-add-size, 2.75rem);
    padding: 0;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .product-card__quick-add--icon .quick-add__label {
    position: absolute;
    inline-size: 1px;
    block-size: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* The cart icon: 45% of the 44px circle (~20px; quick-add's own share is 35%) */
  .product-card .product-card__quick-add:not(.product-card__cart-text) .quick-add__cart {
    inline-size: calc(var(--quick-add-size, 50px) * 0.45);
    block-size: calc(var(--quick-add-size, 50px) * 0.45);
  }

  /* A very narrow card (320px phones, 2 per row: a 105px row): BUY without its icon, a smaller circle */
  @container product-card (max-width: 9.5rem) {
    .product-card .product-card__buy-link {
      padding-inline: 0.75rem;
    }

    .product-card .product-card__buy-link :is(svg, img) {
      display: none;
    }

    /* 40px (quick-add writes its own 44px size inline, so the size is set on the button itself) */
    .product-card .product-card__quick-add--icon .quick-add__button {
      inline-size: 2.5rem;
      block-size: 2.5rem;
    }

    .product-card__buy-now {
      gap: 0.375rem;
    }
  }

  /* Medium: options on the left of the cart + BUY row */
  @container product-card (min-width: 15rem) {
    .product-card--full .product-card__body {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      grid-template-areas:
        'meta meta'
        'title title'
        'price price'
        'options buy';
      align-items: center;
    }

    .product-card--full .product-card__meta {
      grid-area: meta;
    }

    .product-card--full .product-card__title {
      grid-area: title;
    }

    .product-card--full .product-card__pricing {
      grid-area: price;
    }

    .product-card--full .product-card__options {
      grid-area: options;
    }

    .product-card--full .product-card__buy {
      grid-area: buy;
      align-self: end;
      padding-block-start: 0;
    }

    /* No options: the buttons take the whole row, BUY still on the right */
    .product-card--full .product-card__body:not(:has(.product-card__options)) {
      grid-template-areas:
        'meta meta'
        'title title'
        'price price'
        'buy buy';
    }
  }

  /*
    Large, with a mouse: options, then price + BUY in one row. The cart button leaves the row and sits
    over the bottom of the photo (its bottom edge = the photo's height, from --card-media-h x the card
    width, less 1.75rem, so it stays above the photo dots at any button height: top there, then
    translate -100%), shown while the card is hovered, while it has keyboard focus and while it adds
  */
  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    @container product-card (min-width: 15rem) {
      .product-card--full .product-card__body {
        grid-template-areas:
          'meta meta'
          'title title'
          'options options'
          'price buy';
      }

      .product-card--full .product-card__body:not(:has(.product-card__options)) {
        grid-template-areas:
          'meta meta'
          'title title'
          'price buy';
      }

      .product-card--full .product-card__buy {
        position: static;
      }

      .product-card--full :is(.product-card__buy-link, .product-card__notify) {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 2;
      }

      .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add {
        position: absolute;
        inset-block-start: calc(var(--card-media-h, 1.25) * 100cqi - 1.75rem);
        inset-inline: 0;
        z-index: 4;
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        pointer-events: none;
        opacity: 0;
        translate: 0 calc(-100% + 0.5rem);
        transition:
          opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out),
          translate var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
      }

      .product-card--full:hover .product-card__quick-add,
      .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add:focus-within,
      .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add:is(.is-adding, .is-added, .is-resetting, .is-error) {
        opacity: 1;
        translate: 0 -100%;
      }

      .product-card--full:hover .product-card__quick-add .quick-add__button,
      .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add:focus-within .quick-add__button {
        pointer-events: auto;
      }

      /* The design's red pill with the cart icon and "ADD TO CART" (also for the "round" style) */
      .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add .quick-add__button {
        inline-size: auto;
        block-size: auto;
        min-block-size: 2.75rem;
        padding-inline: 1.25rem;
        gap: var(--space-xs);
        background-color: var(--color-button);
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-button);
        color: var(--color-button-text);
        font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
      }

      .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add .quick-add__button:hover {
        background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-button) 88%, #000000);
        color: var(--color-button-text);
      }

      .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add--icon .quick-add__label {
        position: static;
        inline-size: auto;
        block-size: auto;
        clip-path: none;
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .product-card--full .product-card__quick-add {
          translate: 0 -100%;
          transition: none;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  /*
    Cart button with text (Theme settings > Product cards > Cart button style): two pills, side by side
    when they fit, else one under the other at full width. Both 44px tall at least (touch target).
  */
  .product-card__buy-now--text {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .product-card__buy-now--text > * {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .product-card__buy-now--text .product-card__buy-link {
    min-block-size: 2.75rem;
  }

  /* Three classes: beat quick-add's pill rule (two classes) and the theme's button[type="submit"] */
  .product-card .product-card__cart-text .quick-add__button {
    inline-size: 100%;
    max-inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
    min-block-size: 2.75rem;
    padding-inline: 1em;
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-align: center;
    white-space: normal;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* The tile panel: the pill as wide as its text */
  .product-card__actions .product-card__cart-text .quick-add__button {
    inline-size: auto;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
  /**
   * <card-options> (full product card): a size pill or colour dot was chosen. Swaps the price (the
   * value's <template>), the "Save" pill, the cart button's variant and name, and the BUY link; a
   * sold-out value hides cart + BUY and shows "Notify me". One AbortController for the editor re-attach.
   */
  class CardOptions extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      this.controller?.abort();
      this.controller = new AbortController();
      this.addEventListener('change', (event) => this.choose(event.target, true), { signal: this.controller.signal });
      // The cart button was rendered with its own first variant: start in step with the checked value
      // (the photo stays: the first photo is the product's, not moved on page load)
      const checked = this.querySelector('input[type="radio"]:checked');
      if (checked) this.choose(checked, false);
    }

    /**
     * Shows the chosen value's photo: its slide when it is one of the first 5, else the photo from its
     * <template> in place of the first slide (or the only photo). The first photo comes back when its
     * own value is chosen again
     */
    showMedia(id) {
      if (!id) return;
      const card = this.closest('.product-card');
      const gallery = card?.querySelector('card-gallery');
      const slides = gallery ? [...gallery.querySelectorAll('.product-card__slide')] : [];
      const index = slides.findIndex((slide) => slide.dataset.mediaId === id);
      const holder = slides[0] || card?.querySelector('.product-card__media');
      const image = holder?.querySelector('.image');

      // This value's photo is already the swapped-in one: just show it
      if (this.swapped?.id === id) {
        gallery?.go(0);
        return;
      }
      if (this.swapped) {
        // Put the first photo back before showing another one
        image?.replaceWith(this.swapped.image);
        this.swapped = null;
      }
      if (index >= 0) {
        gallery.go(index);
        return;
      }
      const template = this.querySelector(`template[data-media-for="${id}"]`);
      const current = holder?.querySelector('.image');
      if (!template || !current) return;
      this.swapped = { id, image: current };
      current.replaceWith(template.content.cloneNode(true));
      gallery?.go(0);
    }

    disconnectedCallback() {
      this.controller?.abort();
    }

    choose(input, showPhoto) {
      if (input.type !== 'radio') return;
      const id = input.value;
      if (showPhoto) this.showMedia(input.dataset.mediaId);

      // No templates = every value costs the same: the price stays
      const price = this.querySelector('[data-card-price]');
      const template = this.querySelector(`template[data-price-for="${id}"]`);
      if (price && template) price.replaceChildren(template.content.cloneNode(true));

      // The "Save 24%" pill and the "-24%" badge on the photo (outside this element) show the same number
      const percent = Number(input.dataset.save) || 0;
      const discounts = [this.querySelector('[data-card-save]'), this.closest('.product-card')?.querySelector('[data-card-discount]')];
      discounts.forEach((element) => {
        if (!element) return;
        element.hidden = percent === 0;
        element.textContent = (element.dataset.template || '').replace('[percent]', percent);
      });

      const quickAdd = this.querySelector('quick-add');
      if (quickAdd) {
        quickAdd.dataset.variantId = id;
        const field = quickAdd.querySelector('input[name="id"]');
        if (field) field.value = id;
        // The round button is named by its aria-label; the text pill by its visible text + a hidden
        // product name (no aria-label: the name must start with the visible text)
        const button = quickAdd.querySelector('.quick-add__button');
        const name = button?.querySelector('[data-quick-add-name]');
        if (name) name.textContent = `: ${input.dataset.addName}`;
        else button?.setAttribute('aria-label', input.dataset.addLabel);
        quickAdd.dataset.labelAdded = input.dataset.addedLabel;
      }

      const link = this.querySelector('[data-card-buy-link]');
      if (link) link.href = `${this.dataset.cartUrl}/${id}:1`;

      const available = input.dataset.available === 'true';
      const buy = this.querySelector('[data-card-buy]');
      if (buy) buy.hidden = !available;
      const notify = this.querySelector('[data-card-notify]');
      if (notify) notify.hidden = available;
    }
  }

  if (!customElements.get('card-options')) customElements.define('card-options', CardOptions);

  /**
   * <card-gallery> (full card with 2+ photos): the track scrolls sideways (swipe, snap points); the
   * arrows (mouse, on hover) and the dots move it one photo. The dots follow the scroll. The next photo
   * is loaded early (when the pointer enters the card, on a touch, and after each move): a lazy image in
   * a sideways track only loads once it is scrolled into view, so the first swipe showed an empty slide.
   * One AbortController for the editor re-attach.
   */
  class CardGallery extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      this.controller?.abort();
      this.controller = new AbortController();
      const { signal } = this.controller;
      this.track = this.querySelector('[data-card-slides]');
      if (!this.track) return;
      this.slides = [...this.track.children];
      this.dots = [...this.querySelectorAll('[data-card-dot]')];
      this.index = 0;

      this.track.addEventListener(
        'scroll',
        () => {
          if (this.frame) return;
          this.frame = requestAnimationFrame(() => {
            this.frame = null;
            this.update();
          });
        },
        { signal, passive: true }
      );

      this.addEventListener(
        'click',
        (event) => {
          const dot = event.target.closest('[data-card-dot]');
          if (dot) this.go(Number(dot.dataset.cardDot));
          else if (event.target.closest('[data-card-prev]')) this.go(this.index - 1);
          else if (event.target.closest('[data-card-next]')) this.go(this.index + 1);
        },
        { signal }
      );

      const card = this.closest('.product-card') || this;
      card.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => this.warm(this.index + 1), { signal });
      this.track.addEventListener('touchstart', () => this.warm(this.index + 1), { signal, passive: true });
    }

    disconnectedCallback() {
      this.controller?.abort();
      if (this.frame) cancelAnimationFrame(this.frame);
      this.frame = null;
    }

    /** The photo in view (scrollLeft is negative in right-to-left pages) */
    update() {
      const width = this.track.clientWidth || 1;
      const index = Math.min(this.slides.length - 1, Math.round(Math.abs(this.track.scrollLeft) / width));
      if (index === this.index) return;
      this.index = index;
      this.dots.forEach((dot, i) => dot.classList.toggle('is-active', i === index));
      this.warm(index + 1);
    }

    /** Moves to a photo; past the last one it goes back to the first (and the other way round) */
    go(index) {
      const count = this.slides.length;
      const target = (index + count) % count;
      const rtl = getComputedStyle(this.track).direction === 'rtl';
      const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      this.warm(target);
      this.track.scrollTo({ left: target * this.track.clientWidth * (rtl ? -1 : 1), behavior: reduced ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
    }

    /** Loads one photo now (lazy images in a sideways track wait until they are scrolled into view) */
    warm(index) {
      const image = this.slides[index]?.querySelector('img');
      if (image && image.loading === 'lazy') image.loading = 'eager';
    }
  }

  if (!customElements.get('card-gallery')) customElements.define('card-gallery', CardGallery);
{% endjavascript %}
